---
source: crates/detoxrs/tests/help_snapshot.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8(out.stdout).expect(\"help is UTF-8\")"
---
Make filenames sane: unix-safe, portable, readable. Preview by default.

Usage: detoxrs [OPTIONS] <PATH>...

Arguments:
  <PATH>...
          Files and/or directories to clean

Options:
  -x, --exec
          Perform the renames (not implemented in this build)

  -n, --dry-run
          Preview only; explicit form of the default

  -r, --recursive
          Descend into directories; without it, a directory argument has only its own name cleaned

      --on-collision <POLICY>
          What to do when two names want the same destination

          Possible values:
          - number: Insert `-N` before the extension, smallest free `N >= 2`
          - skip:   Leave every colliding entry alone and report it
          - fail:   Refuse the entire batch
          
          [default: number]

  -v, --verbose...
          List unchanged entries too

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only

      --json
          JSON on stdout, diagnostics on stderr

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Nothing is renamed unless you pass -x. This build previews only: -x is parsed but refused, because no write path exists in it yet.

Without -r, a directory argument has only its own name cleaned and nothing inside it is touched (detox differs).

Exit codes:
  0  preview produced with no errors
  2  usage, walk, or plan error
